-- Seed pruned 2021 Census denominators for per-capita location rates.
--
-- Sources (StatCan, 2021 Census, boundaries Jan 1 2021):
--   98-10-0005-01 "Population and dwelling counts: Canada, provinces and
--     territories, census metropolitan areas and census agglomerations"
--     -> metro (CMA), province, country, and province-wide scope buckets.
--     https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/tbl/csv/98100005-eng.zip
--   98-10-0002-01 "Population and dwelling counts: Canada and census
--     subdivisions (municipalities)"
--     -> city buckets (municipality / city proper, CSD level).
--     https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/tbl/csv/98100002-eng.zip
--
-- Pruning (everything not needed for a bucket is dropped):
--   * kept only 2021 population + DGUID; all dwelling counts, land area,
--     density, ranks, and % change columns discarded;
--   * kept only geographies that occur as a location bucket over active
--     jobs: 15 CMAs, 13 provinces, Canada, 13 province-wide scope keys,
--     and 448 city buckets;
--   * city matching prefers the CSD (municipality) row in the job's
--     province; amalgamated boroughs map to their parent municipality
--     (East York/North York/Etobicoke/Scarborough -> Toronto,
--     Kanata/Nepean -> Ottawa, Dartmouth/Cole Harbour -> Halifax,
--     Saint-Laurent/Saint-Hubert -> Montreal/Longueuil, ...); "St."
--     spellings map to StatCan "Saint-" names; see note column.
--   * deliberately seedless (NULL population -> UI shows raw counts):
--     Unspecified, Province-wide, foreign scopes (Boston, New York),
--     reserves/RCMs/regions with no usable CSD, and buckets whose only
--     namesake is a tiny place in another province (Bath ON, Gladstone
--     MB, Trenton ON, Waterville NS, Windsor NS, ...).
-- Full redo instructions live in docs/census-per-capita-methodology.md.

